# Impeccable — machine-local artifacts. The shared design contract (DESIGN.md, PRODUCT.md,
# .impeccable/design.json, .impeccable/config.json) is committed; per-developer state is not.
.impeccable/config.local.json
.impeccable/live/
.impeccable/cache/

# Claude Code per-machine settings (the design hook lives here)
.claude/settings.local.json

# mongod binary cached by CI (MONGOMS_DOWNLOAD_DIR in .github/workflows/ci.yml)
.mongodb-binaries/

# Root-level catch-alls. The leading slash anchors each to the repo root on purpose: an unanchored
# `.env*` would also match server/.env.example, which must stay committed.
/.env
/.env.*
/node_modules/

# OS and editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~

# Markdown is ignored by default so scratch notes and generated reports stay out, but every
# document the repository treats as a contract is negated back in below.
#
# ⚠️ Keep this list in step with the `.impeccable/` block above, which states that DESIGN.md and
# PRODUCT.md are committed — an unqualified `*.md` silently contradicted it, and CLAUDE.md tells
# every session to read DESIGN.md before touching UI. A doc that is not in a fresh clone cannot be
# an implementation contract.
#
# ⚠️ Negation cannot rescue a file whose parent directory is excluded. These all work because only
# `*.md` is ignored here, never `docs/`.
*.md
!README.md
!*/README.md
!CLAUDE.md
!DESIGN.md
!PRODUCT.md
!SECURITY.md
!docs/**/*.md
